{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Abu Dawud","section":{"9":{"eng-name":"Zakat (Kitab Al-Zakat)","ara-name":"كتاب الزكاة"}},"section_detail":{"9":{"hadithnumber_first":1556,"hadithnumber_last":1700,"arabicnumber_first":1556,"arabicnumber_last":1700}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":1558,"arabicnumber":1558,"text":"Rapporté par Abu Sa’id Al Khudri : L’Envoyé d’Allah ﷺ a dit : « Il n’y a pas de zakat à payer pour moins de cinq chameaux, moins de cinq onces d’argent, et moins de cinq charges de chameau (wasq). »","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Bukhari (1447) Sahih Muslim (979)"}],"reference":{"book":9,"hadith":3},"chapter":{"id":2,"ara-name":"باب مَا تَجِبُ فِيهِ الزَّكَاةُ","eng-name":"Property On Which Zakat Is Payable","isFirstHadith":true}}]}